## Static and PURE scope

The independent reader derives the source delta, 34-table export topology, 4,044 parent and 4,044 predicted child report cells, five paired changes, all four predeclared full-log forms, and the source-ready/assigned/in-transit/location ledger without author validator imports. Its JSON decoder rejects duplicate keys, NaN/Infinity and exponent overflow; native report normalization permits only the single declared trailing comma. It binds 76 accepted disk/base-Git identities, 114 mandatory historical original raw files, eight documents, three installed assets, distinct owned local/Git catalog archives, the typed 496-entry live prefix, 43 context copies and 26 local PURE-proof copies.

The sealed branch requires the final independently closed **119-path** owned inventory, every manifest source byte pin, fresh preflight/approval, five captured original-stream PURE helpers, exact six-stage program/argv/PID/session/integer exit/UTC/source-map chain, all 25 original native files and 23 closure raw pins, converter log triple seal, exact checker receipts, and the independent source/event/report gates. `--evidence-dir` reads a byte-identical recovered copy after requiring the original run and all 25 original file pins. No recovered copy can replace a missing original.

PURE fixture and self-check exited zero in local review: four positive transcript forms, 8,088 one-cell report mutations rejected, and 76 additional semantic/protocol mutations rejected. The distinct synthetic checker CLI bridge at `tmp/i04-var03-checker-bridge-v1-20261008/receipt.json` records original stdout/stderr bytes: run-directory invocation passed and a bool-valued double cell was rejected. These are predicted fixtures, not SIMLOX observations. The author's first converter PURE script failed because its local test used `Get-FileHash` in an isolated PS5 scope; the revised local test uses .NET SHA256. Production runner still uses `Get-FileHash`, so actual SSH5 preflight must prove it on the real path.

Next gate: root captures the exact frozen reader/self-check original binary output, writes canonical inventory and manifest once, and requests a separate GO_PURE_PREFLIGHT on those bytes. Native launch remains unapproved.
